      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please add a line break to make it obvious is not part of the 2 before (I know there is a dot)\nOr maybe a list item :\n```\n/// Thus, FFI can be either:\n///  * Rust to C++\n///  * C++ to Rust\n///     * Core C++ to Rust only via injected callbacks (libbluetooth-core does not depend on libbluetooth_core_rs)\n///     * Profile C++ to Rust can be made directly (as libbluetooth *does* depend on libbluetooth_core_rs).\n```\n\n\nAlso, you mention 2 different c++ for c++ \u003d\u003e rust but you don\u0027t make this distinction in Rust\u003d\u003eC++.\nI understand this mean rust \u003d\u003e c++ core as rust depend on the bluetooth_core, and the rust\u003d\u003e c++ profile is only with callback. (like any core -\u003e profile)",
